From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:21:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dspark): allow PIECEWISE adaptive verification and
 filter dead rows from expert-slot lookahead

Remove the legacy full-CUDA-graph restriction from VllmConfig._validate_adaptive_verification and resolve_adaptive_cudagraph_mode (obsolete under the deterministic analytic row_cost model), and filter dead/padding rows (topk_ids < 0) out of ExpertSlotCache RouterLookaheadPredictor so NVMe-offloaded TP1/TP2 shapes never prefetch experts for pruned draft tails. Zero behavior or graph change on FULL_AND_PIECEWISE / FULL_DECODE_ONLY (TP3..TP8).

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Unlocks NVMe-calibrated PIECEWISE adaptive verification on TP1 (+64.6% c1 to 5.733 tok/s, -34.5% TPOT, +82.9% c4 to 5.425 tok/s, 89.2% vs 29.9% draft efficiency across 2 boots on dgx4).
Quality: 2,048/2,048 greedy output tokens and top-20 logprobs bit-exact vs fixed drafts=5 and drafts=0 (rank1=1.0, perplexity=1.3209161, 0 diffs).
Tests: tests/test_config.py, tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py, and 13-run live dgx4 screen (PR #1289).
Upstream-status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 adaptive verification and expert-slot offload patch.
